    "state": "open",
    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "[RFC] build: Configuration macro names are susceptible to typos",
    "body": "We currently define and use configuration macros as follows:\n\n```cpp\n// build/src/bitcoin-build-config.h\n#define HAVE_FOO 1\n/* #undef HAVE_BAR */\n```\n\n```cpp\n// some source file\n#include <bitcoin-build-config.h> // IWYU pragma: keep\n...\n#ifdef HAVE_FOO\n...\n#endif // HAVE_FOO\n...\n#ifndef HAVE_BAR\n...\n#endif // HAVE_BAR\n\n```\n\nThis is susceptible to typos. A misspelt name, e.g. `#ifdef HAVE_F0O`, compiles cleanly and silently disables the guarded code. None of our tools catches it, neither the compiler with `-Wundef` nor the linter.\n\nRelated: #16419, #29876, #36023.",
